do_1 = "In storage/db_engine/litt/disktable/segment/segment.go:130-154, extend constructor failure cleanup to close every successfully opened value shard as well as the key handle before returning a createValueFile error; attempt all closes even if one close fails and report cleanup errors without losing the original constructor error. Preserve the successful ownership transfer at segment.go:169-197 so returned segments retain their writable handles, and leave existing files and their contents intact."
do_2 = "Extend TestRepairM_1162_ConstructorErrors in storage/db_engine/litt/disktable/segment/repair_m1162_test.go:136-148 to exercise real four-shard construction with a pre-existing value file at shard 0, shard 1 and the last shard, both durability modes, and one and multiple segment paths using the placement rule at segment.go:147. Repeat each failure with distinct indices, assert a nil segment and the original already-exists error, preserve the conflicting file contents, and assert zero segment descriptors across every path immediately after each failure using the existing descriptor counter at repair_m1162_test.go:26-42; prevent garbage collection from masking missing explicit closes during these assertions and restore its setting afterward. Retain the existing shard-zero coverage and run TestRepairM_1162_Rotation at repair_m1162_test.go:44-101 to prove successful construction still supports Write, Flush, Seal and reopening with bounded descriptor use."
